Fix: drop inventoryId from stock event payloads (kafka-publish_20261001)

Discovered while implementing Phase 3 (HTTP wiring): InventoryStore.reserve's InsufficientStock result carries no Inventory entity, so there was no id to populate StockReservationFailedEvent.inventoryId with - and order-service (the consumer) never has an inventoryId to correlate against in the first place, only the sku it asked to reserve.

User chose to drop inventoryId from the contract entirely rather than add a lookup or make it optional. Updated: StockEvents.scala (both case classes), StockEventPublisherSuite.scala (test fixtures), and gluon/docs/system-design.md's payload-contracts section (separate commit in the gluon repo, 0b24254).
